    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d662">

                <pb facs="0948" n="820" sameAs="frus:frus1928v01/pg820"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">811.79620 Boeing Airplane Co./2: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to the Ambassador in
                        Brazil</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Morgam</hi>)<anchor n="96"
                        xml:id="d662-f1"/></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1928-02-06T18:00:00-05:00"><hi rendition="#italic">February 6,
                                1928—6 p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>3. Captain Ralph A. O’Neill, representing the Boeing Airplane Company of Seattle,
                    and the Pratt and Whitney Motor Corporation of Hartford, Connecticut, is sailing
                    on S. S. <hi rendition="#italic">Southern Cross</hi> February 11, for Rio de
                    Janeiro for an experimental flight and to demonstrate before army and navy air
                    service.</p>
                <p>Please request free entry for equipment, including Boeing pursuit plane, Boeing
                    mail plane and accessories, and ask permission for flight in Brazil. Reply by
                    cable.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Olds</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d662-f1" n="96" type="source" xml:id="d662-f1-content">
                <p>The same, <hi rendition="#italic">mutatis mutandis</hi>, on the same date to the
                    missions in Argentina (No. 6), Chile (No. 14), Peru (No. 9), and Uruguay (No.
                    2).</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
